# The published SHA256 of frame.txt is taken over the bytes on disk, and the contract
# tells a reader to verify it with `sha256sum frame.txt` after cloning. Git must therefore
# never rewrite its line endings on checkout: with core.autocrlf=true on Windows it did,
# and the published hash failed to verify for every such reader. See DEFECTS.md.
survey-verifier-claims/frame.txt -text

# Same reasoning for anything else whose bytes are committed to by a published digest.
*.txt -text
